                                            1. Let f = (P, Q) : C2(x,y) −→ C2(u,v) be a dominant polynomial map,
                                            P, Q ∈ C[x, y] and denote J(P, Q) := Px Qy − Py Qx . Recall that the so-called
                                            non-proper value set Af of f is the set consists of all point a ∈ C2 such that
