/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/nori-bc-verification-grok46-20260831.md-85-**Bézout and type.** `C_1 ∩ C_2 = {x=0, zy=0} = {P=[0:1:0], Q=[0:0:1]}`, local intersection 2 at each, total 4. Both conics are smooth (the affine `YZ=1` is a smooth hyperbola; the points at infinity on each conic are smooth). Each of `P,Q` is an `A_3` of two smooth branches, contact `2`. For each component: `r_1(C_i)=0`, `T(C_i)=0`, `T_x(C_i)=2+2=4`, `C_i^2=4`. Definition 3.25 sees only branches of `C_i` itself, so `A(C_i;P)=0` and `B(C_i)=C_i^2=4>0`.
