/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/nori-bc-verification-grok46-20260831.md-91-1. *Algebraic identification.* Set `c=t_1 t_λ`. The presentation is `⟨ t_λ, c | c^2=1 ⟩ ≅ Z * Z/2`. The two-relation form `⟨ a,b | (ab)^2=(ba)^2=1 ⟩` is the same group: `(ba)^2 = b(ab)^2 b^{-1}`, so the second relation is redundant once `(ab)^2=1`. Kurosh: the group is nonabelian. Abelianization: `H_1 ≅ Z ⊕ Z/2`, matching the standard `H_1(P^2-D)` for a two-component degree-`(2,2)` curve (`c_1(O(D_i))` generate with the relation `2[C_1]+2[C_2]=0` in `H_2(P^2)`, i.e. `2(t_1+t_λ)=0`).
