/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/nori-bc-verification-grok46-20260831.md-94-   `π_1(CP^2-S) ≅ ⟨ x_1, x_2 | (x_1 x_2)^2 = (x_2 x_1)^2 = e ⟩`.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/nori-bc-verification-grok46-20260831.md-95-   The same isomorphism to `Z * Z/2` is recorded in arXiv:math/0612346v2, Corollary 3.10 and the discussion after Corollary 2.9 (SHA-256 `7287c49c…`): `⟨ a,b | (ab)^2=(ba)^2=e ⟩ ≅ ⟨ x,y | x^2=e ⟩ ≅ Z * Z/2`. Their route is braid monodromy of the real arrangement, not the fibration `YZ` used in the charged report.
